    cultural_note: "Vietnamese rhetoric at the C2 level blends classical persuasion modes with Vietnamese cultural expectations: ethos is built through demonstrated experience, not claimed status; pathos is expressed through acknowledgment of shared concern, not emotional appeal; logos requires explicit structure (thứ nhất, thứ hai, thứ ba) that English rhetoric can sometimes skip.",
    tip: "The Vietnamese rhetorical triad is not ethos-pathos-logos — it is kinh nghiệm (experience), thấu hiểu (understanding), and logic rõ ràng (clear logic). All three must be present in any C2-level persuasive speech.",
